From b5a3e67e7b208b978f1b29803a837236915abfcf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vanshika <pahalvanshikaa@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 02:52:28 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] blt-mcp: enforce strict plain-text output for
 draft_vision_issue

The vision prompt only loosely asked for TITLE/DESCRIPTION sections, so
the model could return Markdown, extra sections, or no markers at all,
and the raw text was passed straight to the TUI.

Rewrite the prompt with a fixed two-field plain-text contract, a
screenshot-only evidence rule and a deterministic no-issue fallback.
Validate the response before returning it: markers must appear once, in
order, with non-empty values. Unusable output now raises a controlled
error instead of being shown as a bug report.

Fixes #24

Signed-off-by: Vanshika <pahalvanshikaa@gmail.com>
